# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/


# Added by cargo

/target

# Iceberg warehouse written by examples/tests
/data

# Custom
.DS_Store

# Internal design notes, and the primary sources they cite. Working documents:
# they quote the regulatory and format sources by clause, and record what each
# design decision cost. `site/` is the public narrative, `CHANGELOG.md` the
# history and the rustdoc the API contract; `concepts/` is none of the three, and
# nothing in the build reads it.
#
# `concepts/references/` holds the sources themselves — statutes, BNetzA
# Festlegungen, EDI@Energy documents, BDEW Anwendungshilfen, NIST/ENTSO-E
# publications and the Apache format specifications. Third-party publications
# under their own terms, so they are staged rather than committed;
# `just references` rebuilds the folder from the index beside it.
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications and the Spec Kit machinery that
# produces them (`/speckit-*` skills, templates, `.specify/memory/constitution.md`).
# Same rule as `concepts/`: internal, and every specification is named by an item
# in the roadmap there, so neither half means anything without the other.
/specs/
/.specify/

# The checker `just concepts` runs over `concepts/` and `specs/`. It tests the
# design notes' own rules and nothing tracked, so it goes where they go.
/tools/

# Agent skills. The procedure for working this repository, which reads
# `concepts/` on every phase and is meaningless without it — so it is ignored for
# the same reason `concepts/` is. `AGENTS.md` is committed, because it is what an
# agent needs before touching code and that is true whether or not the design
# notes are present.
/.claude/

# Built documentation site (see .github/workflows/site.yml).
site/public/
